2. Used, not distributed with STEEL
-----------------------------------

faster-whisper (speech to text), MIT License.
  https://github.com/SYSTRAN/faster-whisper
  Installed into the OpenJarvis environment; imported by STEEL's voice code.

Whisper models, MIT License.
  OpenAI Whisper (https://github.com/openai/whisper), in the CTranslate2
  conversions Systran/faster-whisper-small and Systran/faster-whisper-base
  (MIT). Downloaded by the owner; revisions and checksums in docs/VOICE.md.

onnxruntime, MIT License.
  https://github.com/microsoft/onnxruntime
  Loaded by faster-whisper (voice detection) and by Piper. It contains
  Microsoft telemetry, which STEEL switches off with ORT_DISABLE_TELEMETRY=1
  (docs/VOICE.md section 3).

Piper (piper-tts 1.8.0), GNU General Public License v3.0 or later.
  https://github.com/OHF-Voice/piper1-gpl (it includes espeak-ng, also
  GPL-3.0-or-later).
  Used as a separate program: STEEL starts it from its own virtual
  environment and talks to it only through pipes. STEEL does not import,
  copy or distribute Piper (docs/SPEAK.md section 4). Anyone who distributes
  Piper together with STEEL takes on the GPL's obligations for Piper.


3. Voices (downloaded by scripts/speak_setup.py, not in this repository)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------

From https://huggingface.co/rhasspy/piper-voices at revision
5041a7a49ae5b3a0f30e6837769eb03fdbb231bd. A voice's licence is that of the
recordings it was trained on (docs/SPEAK.md section 3).

en_US-john-medium
  Recordings from LibriVox (https://librivox.org): public domain.
  Fine-tuned from the "kristin" voice (LibriVox, public domain).

es_ES-carlfm-x_low
  Recordings from https://github.com/carlfm01/my-speech-datasets:
  public domain.

